drm/panel: nt36523: Remove the panel when DSI attach fails.

The probe added the panel and returned on a failed DSI attach without
removing it. The panel lives in devm memory, so it was freed while still
in the panel list; the touch driver then found it as its panel to
follow, and its unwind oopsed in drm_panel_remove_follower (issue #24).

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36523.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36523.c
@@ -1250,8 +1250,15 @@
 		pinfo->dsi[i]->mode_flags = pinfo->desc->mode_flags;
 
 		ret = devm_mipi_dsi_attach(dev, pinfo->dsi[i]);
-		if (ret < 0)
+		if (ret < 0) {
+			/*
+			 * The panel is freed with the device's resources:
+			 * leaving it listed let a follower (the touch screen)
+			 * find it and use freed memory.
+			 */
+			drm_panel_remove(&pinfo->panel);
 			return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "cannot attach to DSI%d host.\n", i);
+		}
 	}
 
 	return 0;
